35,2,1,talk,Midori,,The board minutes show a joint clinic failed because neither department held the budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The readmission trial worked, but the data agreements take fourteen months to sign.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Ward vacancies are high, but midwifery has unusual slack due to falling births.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The development budget is down a quarter, and off-site visits earn no tariff.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Outpatient rooms are full by mid-morning, and the shuttle misses most villages.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we fund home care?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Misaki, the midwifery slack is interesting. Could that support a perinatal program?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Yes, but the therapy staff are leaving for city posts. That is a risk.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,The ledger is tight. We cannot afford to build new spaces for therapy.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,The booking system only records fixed slots. Home visits would disappear from reports.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,The shared nursing round lost a third of visits. Home follow-up might be too fragile.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The data agreement delay makes chronic care coordination very slow to start.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,Perinatal support uses existing midwifery slack. It seems the most feasible.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Day rehabilitation requires new space, which the budget cannot cover.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,Perinatal classes can use existing rooms if scheduled carefully. It fits the flow.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,I am leaning towards the option that uses existing staff slack.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. The perinatal service seems the most grounded in current reality.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,The staffing data supports the perinatal option.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,It is the only one that does not require new capital expenditure.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It fits into the day without seizing up the system.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
